Finding: {"title":"GET /micamp/admin/schools does an in-memory N-table join instead of a SQL join, and returns processing fee percent + merchant key for every school with no pagination","severity":"LOW","area":"Performance / scalability","files":["src/server/routes/routes-micamp.ts"],"detail":"L771-811: fetches ALL flight schools and ALL micamp configs as two separate full-table scans, then joins them in application memory via a Map. As the number of flight schools grows this becomes an unbounded, unpaginated payload with two full-table reads per request (super-admin only, so lower severity, but still a scalability smell in a route intended to list every tenant on the platform).","impact":"Linear growth in response size and latency as schools onboard; no pagination means the endpoint will eventually become slow or hit response-size limits.","recommendation":"Do a single SQL LEFT JOIN between flightSchools and paymentProcessorConfigs filtered to processor='micamp', and add pagination/limit params once school count grows past a reasonable threshold (e.g. 200).","confidence":"low"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

